      trivia: "【The Band at the Foot】Juan Clemente’s greatest singularity lies in its inverted device: the band wound not at the head but at the foot of the cigar, with the foot covered in foil. It was not mere eccentricity but served the practical end of protecting the delicate foot from cracking — an expression of the founder’s insistence on perfect construction.【A Name Transformed】Jean Clément, a Frenchman born in Champagne, Hispanicised his own name to christen the marque “Juan Clemente”. The founder died in New Orleans in 2010, in the midst of the trade show where the industry gathers."
