      trivia: "【The Master Who Nearly Became a Drummer】Ernesto Perez-Carrillo Jr., the master blender who stands for modern Dominican cigars, aspired in his youth to be a jazz drummer, crossing to New York at 25 to make his way as a musician. He is said to have gone to every length to join the band of the great tenor player Stan Getz, failed, and returned to Miami to take over his father’s El Credito factory. Had he succeeded in jazz, neither the Encore of 2018 nor the Pledge of 2020 might ever have been born. Fittingly, the factory bearing his name has been renamed from La Alianza, meaning “alliance”, to Casa Carrillo, the family “house” — a return to a name that mirrors the family’s story."
